# PY-1: 1.37.1 vs master on py-fastapi.
# A = 1.37.1 (9c034c47), B = master ed75ffa14, which has 0daef33c
# "http: compress application responses of unknown length".
# One app process; counts only, on a 2-CPU box with a PMU.
JOB=py1-fastapi
REV_A=9c034c47765fc448ba0ae3787285b48644b65e4d
REV_B=ed75ffa14f2a2fe5281fbe0eb132f88e50a117a2
WORKLOAD=py-fastapi
CONNS=1 32
WARM=2
DUR=8
REPS=2
APP_PROCS=1
PERF=1
STRACE=1
PRIMARY=r_instructions
EXPECT=A and B level (NO CLAIM) on r_instructions: JSONResponse sets content-length, so the 0daef33c path is not taken; the framework share shows in s_instructions, not in the router
FALSIFY=null band over 5 percent; or a CLAIM on r_instructions (then something other than 0daef33c moved the router between 1.37.1 and master)
